Brick: turn off PowerVR Active Power Management by default.

APM powers the GPU down after a few seconds idle. The A133 GPU power
domain on this kernel cannot complete a non-forced power-off ("GPU power
failure at non-forced OFF did not reach HOST; reboot required"), which
latches the GPU until reboot after the first GL app exits. Keep it on.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/config_kernel.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/img/img-rogue/config_kernel.h
@@ -76,3 +76,3 @@
 #define PVRSRV_APPHINT_KCCB_SIZE_LOG2 7
-#define PVRSRV_APPHINT_ENABLEAPM RGX_ACTIVEPM_DEFAULT
+#define PVRSRV_APPHINT_ENABLEAPM RGX_ACTIVEPM_FORCE_OFF
 #define PVRSRV_APPHINT_ENABLEHTBLOGGROUP 0
